        "wheelMoves": 4,
        "method": "wheel",
        "endingText": "bandon convenience, but reintroduce deliberate friction where it creates meaning: moments of discovery, creative tension, shared experiences and niche cultural relevance.\n\nSuccess will belong to the brands that understand shopping is no longer a straight line to checkout. It’s a cycle of emotional engagement, where attention must be earned, not bought — and loyalty is a result, not a goal.\n\nThe funnel is broken. Now, it’s up to marketers to decide whether they’ll keep optimising for the past, or start building the future.\n\nFuture\nMeaning\nDiscovery\n\nThis is the second installment of a two‑part series on how Gen Z Broke the Marketing Funnel, produced in partnership with youth culture agency Archrival, who provided research, insights, and design.\n\nCheck out the first report here.\n\nBACK TO TOP"
      },
